<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Checks the minimap's and the GPS's game-free parts outside the game: the search done whole and in slices, routes
       on a made-up grid of streets, turns, leaving the route and arriving, the view's arithmetic and the map picture.
       Compiles the mod's own files, so it checks exactly what ships. It also checks the bus bays (BayCheck.cs with
       Transport\BusBay.cs): where a bus stands, the curves in and out, and a model bus driven along them. And the taxi called from the
       phone (TaxiCheck.cs with Transport\Taxi\TaxiRules.cs): its charges, its bands, its refusals, and its search. And the rules of the live street
       (StreetCheck.cs with Traffic\Reckless\StreetRules.cs): the horn, the reckless drivers, how often, and what comes of it. And the minimap's
       buildings and water (BaseCheck.cs with Navigation\NavBaseRules.cs): a place on the picture and back, the window at the city's edges,
       outlines, the water grid, the drawing and the kept file. And three small rules
       of the interface and the camera (PolishCheck.cs with Core\GameUi\PanelPlacement.cs, Core\GameUi\BarRule.cs, Camera\CameraWatch.cs and
       Core\OtherModName.cs): where a panel stands beside the game's building box, when a bar is written again, and when the camera
       stands down for another mod's. And the ambulance crew's way as geometry (CrewCheck.cs with People\CrewPath.cs): how near the
       crew comes to a point and to a length of tape, and what a planning's worth of ways costs. And the game-free parts of the work against long frames (HitchCheck.cs and HotSpotCheck.cs with Core\EventHold.cs, Core\WorkRings.cs, Core\HotSpots.cs and Core\SearchPace.cs): handlers kept on the game's events, the session record's rings, the timing of the mod's own scripts by feature and method, when the whole scene may be searched (DoorFadeCheck.cs: on a model of the game's own fades at a door and in a taxi, frame by frame, only on a frame its black screen covers at full strength), and (PrewarmCheck.cs, over the sources) that the one-off work of the first seconds after a load is handed to the loading screen or read from the game's own lists. And getting out of the driving school's car (CarExitCheck.cs with Licences\Driving\CarExitRules.cs): the places tried around the car, when a player is stuck half out of it, and when the car may go. And the driving school's route (TestRouteCheck.cs with Licences\Driving\TestRouteRules.cs): planned round lanes an accident has closed, the car's lane shut and the other way open, a road that leads nowhere, and what the player is told. And the furnished police station (StationCheck.cs with Law\StationGrid.cs): the walkway check that keeps the counter, the cell and every seat reachable from the door, and how many people the station has. And the tow truck (TowCheck.cs with Traffic\Tow\TowRules.cs): its bed's motion, a wreck drawn along the road and up the bed without a jump, where it stands ahead of a wreck, how long it is said to take, and when it may come and go. And the tech sector's buildings (TechSiteCheck.cs with Tech\Sites\SitePlan.cs and RoomPlans.cs): a data centre's server room by tier and racks, its aisles and walkways, a headquarters' lobby, a tech office's fittings, and the tech companies' towers (TowerCheck.cs with Tech\Sites\HqTowers.cs and Core\SpecialNameBook.cs): which office buildings house the companies, a floor each, the floors at a door and the lift, the buildings back on the market, and the desk on the employer's floor. And the fit-out of the mod's buildings (FitCheck.cs with FitOut\FitRules.cs, FitPlanner.cs and FitPlanner.Zones.cs): the game's design for a unit round what a building already has, the bare floor given rooms of the building's kind, and the walkway check that keeps every seat, every way out and every part of the floor reached from the door; and where the player stands to sit at their desk (DeskReachCheck.cs with FitOut\DeskReach.cs): out of the chair away from its desk, never under it, and a desk that cannot be walked to from the door passed over for the next one round. And whose a car is in a Going Public session (CarCheck.cs with Core\WhoseCar.cs): another player's car is never the player's to tow, impound or bill for, and a car of the traffic pool is asked for only when the game would take an idle one of that very prefab, never one in use by its model. And the fronts of the mod's buildings (FrontSignCheck.cs with Core\FrontSignRules.cs and Core\SpecialNameBook.cs): no "For rent" on a building the mod has made its own, its company's or institution's sign in its own colours on the game's sign holders (one sign each, with the boards and the police stations' and hotels' dressing), the city map's rows of units to let and for sale without them, an unclaimed building as the game has it, and nothing of it written into the save. And the long-frame line's account of a stutter (FrameCheck.cs with Diagnostics\FrameRules.cs): the main thread's own work, a wait for the last frame to be shown, another program or time outside the engine's steps, and the words for each. And what a long session keeps (MemoryCheck.cs with Diagnostics\ObjectKinds.cs): the session record's count of the mod's objects by holder and by kind, what grew the most since the first minute, and a bounded number of kinds; and (with Core\CacheRules.cs) a record of the game's pooled people that starts again once it has outgrown the pools. And the first second after a save loads (StartCheck.cs with Core\StartRules.cs and Diagnostics\FrameRules.cs): the directors' first loads one a frame, in the order they ran in before whatever order the engine runs their timers in, each after the ones it reads, and a frame while the loading screen fades out counted as hidden. And the nearest lane point asked of a grid (PointGridCheck.cs with Core\PointGrid.cs): the same point as the traffic system's pass over every lane point, its filter asked of the same points in the same order, and nothing in the mod asking that pass any more. And bicycles and motorbikes (BikeCheck.cs with Garage\BikeRules.cs): a bicycle's pull-away and cruising speed, the rider's pose without a jump, the lean by speed, the boxes the world meets on the four bikes' own numbers, and over the sources their names and the boxes put on and given back; and where one is left (BikeClearCheck.cs with Garage\BikeClearRules.cs): a bike left over a post found in it and a clear place for it within reach, only the player's own moved, and the check made on every getting off and on, never per frame; and its mass when it is got on (BikeTurnCheck.cs with Garage\BikeRules.cs): the centre of mass and inertia kept only from a body free to turn and written back only into one, on a model of what the game and the mod do to the scooter's body (saved standing or in the saddle and loaded, bought, got off and on, fallen from, held and dressed again), each of the four kinds turning on the game's own inertia whenever it is ridden, the game's hold on a standing bike never undone, and the same model the way before showing a bike that steers and goes straight on after a load. And leisure's reaches (LeisureReachCheck.cs with Leisure\LeisureReach.cs): the chess table, the night's two at a door, the activities' leashes and what is offered where, each in metres against the square of a flat distance, and over the sources every square of a flat distance compared with a square. And a police station's door and front desk (StationReachCheck.cs with Law\StationReach.cs): the panel and its key from the doorstep, as the game lets the player through one of its own doors, never from the kerb, the road or another floor, and over the sources every distance in metres from JobSpots.Flat compared with metres, never a square. And the city's drivers (DriverCheck.cs with Traffic\Drivers\DriverRules.cs and DriverRules.Road.cs): each case driven against a model of the game's own traffic system (its 4.5 m sensor and 1.25 m stop), with the drivers' braking and without: braking in good time and smoothly, the room kept for the player to park, a car letting the player out of a space, and the officer who waves an emergency unit through an accident's open lane (Traffic\CordonRules.cs), the option off giving everything back (over the sources), and what a look costs. And who has the game's one panel box over a place (PanelPickCheck.cs with Core\GameUi\PanelPickRules.cs): the nearer place the player faces, a person met first within talking range, a margin so the box never goes to and fro, the game's own panels left where they are, the key to what the box shows, a person waiting stood clear of other panels' places, and over the sources every panel of the mod's through that rule. And the recorded car sounds (CarSoundCheck.cs with Driving\Sound\CarSoundRules.cs, Driving\CarCatalogue.cs and Garage\GarageCatalogue.cs): the crossfade over every rev of every engine with no gap and no step, load, pops, boost and the turntable's revs, every clip the code names shipped with its licence line, the sound parts' prices and trade-offs, and over the sources every way back to the game's own sound and nothing of traffic, the bus or the tow truck. And when a contact of the player's car is the car hitting something (CarContactCheck.cs with Traffic\CarContactRules.cs and Licences\Driving\TestContactRules.cs): never the road under a van whose nose dips as it brakes, a kerb under the wheels, its load or a trigger; a car, a person, a post, a wall or a tree by the speed into it; and over the sources every collision of that car judged so. And the driven car's handling (HandlingCheck.cs with Driving\HandlingRules.cs, HandlingModel.cs, HandlingTurn.cs, CurveKeys.cs and Garage\GarageCatalogue.cs): on the game's own eighteen cars as its files have them, Empire Motors' two and four cars of other mods (assumed), at every level and with every build of the Garage's springs, weight and tyres, the side grip against the game's own curve, the anti-roll bars, rolling over against what the tyres hold, the damping, every turn the game's car makes with the key held up to its own top speed and the city's corners at the game's speed, the roll, the dive, the steering and the brakes and their ramp; and over the sources every value put back on every way out, what the handling wrote read back before the Garage's parts go on top, and only the driven car touched. And walking on a key (WalkCheck.cs with Walking\WalkRules.cs): the toggle and what stops it, the game's own walk put on over its run or jog and given back, frame by frame on a model of the game's own loop (Toggle Running held and let go, a door, a vehicle left, a job's and Going Public's own speeds never written over, a load), the game's walk cycle at its own rate, and over the sources one key read, nothing sent or saved, the game touched only through WalkGame and the texts in the three languages. And the game's car wash in a repair bay (WashCheck.cs with Garage\WashRules.cs): on a model of the game's own wash frame by frame, a wash that runs never ended by the watch at any frame rate, paused, with a long frame or pressed again at once, and one that stops (another mod's car with no spray, its object switched off) ended once soon after the longest wash, the car and the player let go and the car clean; and over the sources the stand-ins given before the wash can be pressed, the end letting go of all the game's wash takes, and every way out of the custom shop, the Garage's clean-up among them, giving the car and the view back. And somebody seated at the chess table (TableSeatCheck.cs with CityLife\TableSeat.cs): facing the board's centre from either stool at every heading of the table, a body turned off it caught, and over the sources every chess player kept at the table once a second and given back off the stool. And the distance culling of the mod's own things (CullCheck.cs with Performance\CullRules.cs and Performance\CullBook.cs): the game's bands, what may be culled and what never is, the inventory and its files, registrations only from those files and each taken out again, and the culling group's slots; the bounce watch (BounceCheck.cs with Traffic\TrafficWatchRules.cs): a bounce still caught while moving traffic is looked at a fifth as often; the traffic mend (TrafficMendCheck.cs with Traffic\TrafficMendRules.cs): the game's traffic that has stopped adding cars for good told from its own log lines, and given a new density manager within three seconds, never for one bad frame or on a guest, and over the sources the old density manager never read through and no car taken off the road; the picture settings (RenderLevelCheck.cs with Performance\RenderLevelRules.cs): the game's own until moved and their limits; Flare's hour a step a frame (FlareHourCheck.cs with Social\Flare\FlareHourSteps.cs); and the interact key's flags asked only on a press and the bus zones' parking laid out a lane a tick (SlowSpotCheck.cs). Run: dotnet run -c Release (from this folder).
       Exit code 0 = all checks passed. With the path of a file of lane points as its argument it also times the search
       and the picture on that city (see docs/features/navigation.md). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>RealLifeOverhaul</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

